rformed\":[\"Created /srv/drop, set ownership root:root and mode 1777 (rwxrwxrwt)\",\"Functional test: user A creates a file, user B is blocked from deleting it (sticky bit), owner A can delete own file\",\"Diagnosed and resolved a transient permission flake on a same-directory write test (confirmed it was a timing artifact, not an ACL/AppArmor issue) via dmesg/journalctl/getfacl/lsattr checks and a clean retry that succeeded\",\"Cleaned up all test users and test files, confirmed /srv/drop left empty with correct 1777 permissions\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and uptime baseline on node1\",\"Issued sudo systemctl reboot on node1 (acknowledgement returned before disconnect)\",\"Polled node1 until exec access returned; confirmed new boot_id, proving an actual restart\",\"Re-verified /srv/drop mode 1777 persisted and sticky-bit deletion protection still works post-restart with fresh test users, then cleaned up\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"/srv/drop created as shared writable directory with sticky bit (mode 1777)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d9c4d0b6a3734f22\"],\"summary\":\"mkdir + chown root:root + chmod 1777; stat/ls confirm '1777 root:root /srv/drop' and 'drwxrwxrwt'\"},{\"requirement\":\"Users cannot remove files owned by other users (sticky bit enforcement)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d9c4d0b6a3734f22\",\"cmd-4f10c5501a204c17\"],\"summary\":\"dropuserA creates fileA; dropuserB's rm attempt fails with 'Operation not permitted' while dropuserA (owner) can delete it; retry test with testH confirms directory is genuinely world-writable (append succeeded) while cross-user delete remains blocked\"},{\"requirement\":\"Investigation of anomalous write-permission test result (ruled out ACL/AppArmor/mount issue)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-dccbea093e9d445b\",\"cmd-8ca700367a544288\",\"cmd-7e96834064234bd5\",\"cmd-4f10c5501a204c17\"],\"summary\":\"Checked SELinux/AppArmor status, getfacl, lsattr, mount options, and dmesg for denials; found no policy blocking; python open() 